evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT05820152"}, {"study_label": "OPGx-RDH12-1001 LCA (Ph1)", "outcome": "safety and tolerability", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT07681778"}, {"study_label": "Elamipretide panel (NA)", "outcome": "muscle strength", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "42359884"}, {"study_label": "PMD approvals commentary (NA)", "outcome": "FDA approvals for mitochondrial disease therapies", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "42229401"}, {"study_label": "PMD approvals commentary (NA)", "outcome": "sildenafil for Leigh syndrome", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "42229401"}, {"study_label": "ND4 gene therapy meta (Ph2)", "outcome": "BCVA", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42627399"}, {"study_label": "ND4 gene therapy meta (Ph2)", "outcome": "retinal sensitivity", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42627399"}, {"study_label": "ND4 gene therapy meta (Ph2)", "outcome": "quality of life", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42627399"}, {"study_label": "ND4 gene therapy meta (Ph2)", "outcome": "adverse events", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42627399"}, {"study_label": "NR082 RCT (Ph3)", "outcome": "visual acuity", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT07406854"}, {"study_label": "NR082 RCT (Ph3)", "outcome": "safety", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT07406854"}, {"study_label": "NR082 study (Ph2)", "outcome": "safety", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT05293626"}, {"study_label": "NR082 study (Ph2)", "outcome": "visual acuity", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT05293626"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 3, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42495453", "42432986", "NCT05561556"]}, {"intervention": "mitochondrial-targeted agents (multi-drug)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42440741"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42630618"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "stress-related disorders (emotional stress)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["41594657"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "amyotrophic lateral sclerosis", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06429059"]}, {"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 6, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["42415111", "NCT05168774", "NCT07531251", "NCT05162768", "42359884", "42229401"]}, {"intervention": "Calhex231", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42748783"]}, {"intervention": "NAMPT activation (P7C3)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42735786"]}, {"intervention": "AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42709484"]}, {"intervention": "antioxidant/redox-modulating therapies (NAC, elamipretide)", "disease": "retinitis pigmentosa", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42792149"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT05590468"]}, {"intervention": "Nicotinamide riboside", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT05732051"]}, {"intervention": "NR + exercise training", "disease": "AYA HCT survivors", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05194397"]}, {"intervention": "HG004 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06088992"]}, {"intervention": "NFS-02 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT05820152"]}, {"intervention": "OPGx-RDH12-1001", "disease": "LCA-IRD", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT07681778"]}, {"intervention": "ND4 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42627399"]}, {"intervention": "NR082", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07406854", "NCT05293626"]}, {"intervention": "PMD interventional therapies (registry survey)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626"]}], "insights": ["Chronic heart failure: the only statistically significant patient-relevant signal in this record set is a 2026 meta-analysis of mitochondria-targeted agents — LVEF SMD 0.42 vs control (95% CI 0.31–0.53), NYHA improvement RR 2.38, all-cause mortality RR 0.62, HF hospitalizations RR 0.60 (all p<0.05); however, constituent trials are small placebo-controlled Phase-2 RCTs, so superiority versus GDMT (the SOC) is unproven and confidence is limited by placebo-only comparators and small trial sizes (42440741).", "Primary mitochondrial diseases: RCT-level data exist but are unreadable — the Phase-3 elamipretide trial (N=102) and Phase-4 placebo-controlled RCT (N=48) have no posted efficacy results, a systematic trial survey explicitly reports that 'several well-designed late-stage trials have yielded negative or inconclusive outcomes', and a meta-analysis of non-specific antioxidant/metabolic therapies found 'largely negative or mixed results'; supportive care remains the SOC (NCT05162768, NCT07531251, 42361626, 42630618).", "PMD pipeline/regulatory: a trial survey reports 4 therapies with regulatory authorization and a commentary notes two FDA approvals in one year, with elamipretide described as the first treatment indicated for muscle strength in Barth syndrome — but no placebo-controlled efficacy dataset supporting these approvals is posted in this record set, and the only human efficacy-like signal is a single uncontrolled elamipretide case report (LVEF 20%→50%, Ross class IV→I; positive, non-significant, no comparator) (42361626, 42229401, 42359884, 42415111).", "LHON (SOC: idebenone): evidence is preclinical/early-phase only — AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy restored visual function in ND6P25L mice, a meta-analysis of ND4 gene therapy reports positive but non-significant gains in BCVA/retinal sensitivity, and every human trial (NR082 Phase-3 RCT and Phase-2, NFS-02, HG004) has no posted results; no trial is head-to-head against idebenone (42709484, 42627399, NCT07406854, NCT05293626, NCT05820152, NCT06088992).", "Result-absent pipeline: all 14 registered trials in this set lack posted results and are coded direction=unclear — including elamipretide Phase-3/4 RCTs, a small (n=31, pilot) MitoQ-HF placebo-controlled RCT, a non-randomized MitoQ-ALS pilot, an NR+exercise factorial RCT, and first-in-human LHON/LCA-IRD gene-therapy cohorts; the only significant markers on the plot are therefore the HF meta-analysis and preclinical rodent studies (MitoQ, Calhex231, P7C3), leaving the human efficacy-vs-SOC gap unquantified (NCT05162768, NCT07531251, NCT05561556, NCT06429059, NCT05194397, NCT07681778, 42432986, 42748783, 42735786).", "Records excluded from the effect plot as non-interventional (no treatment arm, so no effect estimate vs supportive care): LHON m.11778G>A genetic-architecture analysis (haplogroups D4j/M7/M9/M10 enriched in high-penetrance families; 209 singleton pedigrees suggest the mutation alone is insufficient), a SIRT3 antifibrotic mechanistic review (context-dependent role), and a MitoQ single-cell-omics methods meta-analysis (42632451, 42747679, 40974057)."]}